## Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

- **`POSTGRES_DB`** — Name of the Postgres database
- **`POSTGRES_USER`** — Postgres username
- **`POSTGRES_PASSWORD`** — Postgres password
- **`DB_HOST`** — Hostname of the database service (defaults to `timescaledb` in Docker)
- **`LOG_LEVEL`** — Python logging level (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`). Default: `INFO`

Set `LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` when troubleshooting the consumer's MQTT or database logic.